---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// MOCKUP of the About page after the copy workshop (docs/copy-workshop.md §7).
// Matter-of-fact register (SR §3). The manifesto moves to Reading as an essay.
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Civic Interplay explores how digital and AI methods can support place-based civic enquiry.">

  <article class="about">
    <header class="about-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About Civic Interplay</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        Civic Interplay explores how digital and AI methods can support
        place-based civic enquiry. In the context of AI services and systems,
        it recognises that governing digital infrastructure well, under
        democratic conditions, depends on greater legibility and
        accountability to place-based communities.
      </p>
      <div class="q-note q-pair">
        <p class="q-main">What forms of civic enquiry are possible in an era of AI infrastructure?</p>
      </div>
      <p class="learn"><a href="/proposition/">Read the proposition <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></p>
    </header>



    <section class="fold">
      <details>
        <summary><h2>Projects</h2></summary>
        <div class="fold-body">
      <ul class="doors filled">
        <li class="fill-purple"><a href="/experiments/side-angle-on-place-flows.html"><span>A new kind of archive</span>Tracing public value: A side angle on a place</a></li>
        <li class="fill-ink"><a href="/sovereignties/"><span>Shared records</span>Data Centres Transparency Project</a></li>
        <li class="fill-plum"><a href="/we-care-rmit/"><span>Place</span>WeCare, City North</a></li>
        <li class="fill-terracotta"><a href="/gathering-intelligences/"><span>Method</span>Gathering Intelligences</a></li>
      </ul>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>
    <section class="fold">
      <details>
        <summary><h2>Making value more legible to many</h2></summary>
        <div class="fold-body">
      <p>
        This is a methodology that is in development. Experimentation is
        deliberately open. The purpose is to build a greater sense of agency
        among people who may feel excluded from decisions about how value is
        being captured and shared within their communities.
      </p>
      <p>
        While transparency is never an end in itself, the methods here seek to
        bring attention to the important role that everyday digital
        capabilities play in shaping civic agency, towards more effective
        governance.
      </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="fold">
      <details>
        <summary><h2>On the use of AI</h2></summary>
        <div class="fold-body">
      <p>
        Agents and AI workflows are adopted to read and interrogate information
        records that are publicly available. This includes open government data
        and other information that is available via the public web. The methods
        also establish practices of critical enquiry and sense checking to
        support agents as effective co-enquirers.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI is not supported as a writing tool, wherever possible.
      </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>


    <section class="fold">
      <details>
        <summary><h2>Working with Civic Interplay</h2></summary>
        <div class="fold-body">
      <dl class="stances">
        <div><dt>Public administrations</dt><dd>Read your own plans and priorities against what has been funded, approved and recorded since. The method and the space are open to you; your team runs it. <a href="#contact">Ask about a reading</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Community</dt><dd>Records you can check, and tools for asking your own questions of your place. <a href="/sovereignties/">Explore the Data Centres Transparency Project</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Elected representatives</dt><dd>See the investment and approvals in your area, and what the record shows happened next. <a href="/submission/">Read the Senate submission</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Researchers and educators</dt><dd>The method is open and citable, with datasets on Zenodo. <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/21994643">Records and method on Zenodo</a></dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p id="contact">
        <a class="contact-button" href="https://www.rmit.edu.au/profiles/b/sarah-barns2" data-u="sarah" data-d="studioesem.com" rel="nofollow">Get in touch</a>
      </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>
    <section class="fold">
      <details>
        <summary><h2>Who's behind it</h2></summary>
        <div class="fold-body">
      <div class="lead-person">
        <p>
          Civic Interplay is being explored by <strong><a href="https://sarahbarns.com/">Dr Sarah Barns</a></strong>
          and collaborators, through a <a href="https://www.rmit.edu.au/profiles/b/sarah-barns2">Vice-Chancellor's Senior Research
          Fellowship</a> at RMIT University's
          <a href="https://www.rmit.edu.au/research/centres-collaborations/centre-for-urban-research">Centre for Urban Research</a>.
        </p>
        <img src="/images/partners/rmit-university.png" alt="RMIT University" width="720" height="253" class="rmit" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p>
        Civic Interplay friends and collaborators include the
        <a href="https://fll.pubpub.org/">Futures + Literacies + Methods Lab</a> at
        Utrecht University, Irina Panovich (<a href="https://aiio.studio/">aiio studio</a>),
        Amber Theurer (<a href="https://human-af.com/">HUMAN AF</a>) and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/miguel-mccormick-685a8113/">Miguel
        McCormick</a> (Facta Living Lab, Mexico).
      </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

  </article>

  <style>
    .about {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: var(--fs-label);
      font-weight: var(--w-medium);
      letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--purple);
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    }

    h1 {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 2.8rem);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: 0;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }

    /* The premise, set large: the line the whole practice rests on. */
    .premise-line {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-style: italic;
      font-weight: var(--w-light);
      font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.6vw, 1.55rem);
      line-height: 1.45;
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
      padding-left: 1rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--pink);
    }

    /* Everything after Why now folds away, so the page reads as the
       argument first and the detail on request. */
    .fold {
      margin-top: 0;
      padding-top: 0;
    }

    .fold + .fold {
      border-top-width: 1px;
    }

    .fold details > summary {
      list-style: none;
      cursor: pointer;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 1.4rem 0 0.4rem;
    }

    .fold details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
      display: none;
    }

    .fold summary h2 {
      margin: 0;
    }

    .fold summary::after {
      content: '+';
      flex: none;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      width: 2rem;
      height: 2rem;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 50%;
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--purple);
      background: #fff;
    }

    .fold details[open] > summary::after {
      content: '\2212';
    }

    .fold summary:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--purple);
      outline-offset: 4px;
    }

    .fold-body {
      padding: 0.8rem 0 0.5rem;
    }

    .learn {
      margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
    }

    .learn a {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      font-size: var(--fs-lead);
      color: var(--purple);
      text-underline-offset: 4px;
    }

    .about-head + .fold {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .about-head .q-pair {
      margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    }

    .standfirst + .standfirst {
      margin-top: 0.9rem;
    }

    .standfirst {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-size: var(--fs-lead);
      font-weight: var(--w-light);
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }

    section {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
    }

    h2 {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: var(--fs-h2);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      line-height: 1.2;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }

    p {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-weight: var(--w-light);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }

    p strong {
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--purple);
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .more {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: var(--fs-small);
    }

    .anchors {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }

    .anchors div {
      background: #fff;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--card-shadow);
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    }

    .anchors dt {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: var(--fs-lead);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      color: var(--card-kicker);
      margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    }

    .anchors dd {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-weight: var(--w-light);
      font-size: var(--fs-small);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .lead-person {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 130px;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .rmit {
      width: 130px;
      height: auto;
      margin-top: 0.3rem;
    }

    .lineage {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
      font-size: var(--fs-small);
    }

    .lineage th {
      text-align: left;
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: var(--fs-label);
      font-weight: var(--w-medium);
      letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--text-faint);
      padding: 0 0.8rem 0.5rem 0;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
    }

    .lineage td {
      vertical-align: top;
      padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem 0.6rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-weight: var(--w-light);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lineage td:first-child {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .lineage td:nth-child(2) {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-weight: var(--w-medium);
    }

    .links {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: var(--fs-small);
    }

    .doors {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .doors a {
      display: block;
      background: #fff;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--card-shadow);
      padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .doors a span {
      display: block;
      font-size: var(--fs-label);
      font-weight: var(--w-medium);
      letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--card-kicker);
      margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    }

    /* Projects, filled. Deep inks so white text clears AA. */
    /* Brand purple and the drawing-study ink at full strength; pink and
       terracotta one step deeper so white text clears AA (plum 5.3:1,
       terracotta 4.9:1). */
    .filled .fill-purple     { --fill: var(--purple); --ink: var(--ink-purple); }
    .filled .fill-ink        { --fill: #1f1d24; --ink: #1f1d24; }
    .filled .fill-plum       { --fill: var(--pink); --ink: var(--ink-pink); }
    .filled .fill-terracotta { --fill: var(--terracotta); --ink: var(--ink-terracotta); }

    .doors.filled a {
      background: #fff;
      color: var(--text);
      box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--fill);
    }

    .doors.filled a span {
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .doors.filled a:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--pink);
      outline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .contact-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.55rem 1.2rem;
      background: var(--purple);
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--border);
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-size: var(--fs-small);
      font-weight: var(--w-medium);
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #fff;
    }

    .chain {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.4rem;
      counter-reset: none;
    }

    .chain li {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.4rem;
      background: #fff;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--card-shadow);
      padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    }

    /* The arrow between steps: inquiry leads to literacy, to translation, to agency. */
    .chain li + li::before {
      content: '\2192';
      position: absolute;
      left: -1.25rem;
      top: 0.9rem;
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      color: var(--text-faint);
    }

    .c-name {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
      color: var(--card-kicker);
    }

    .c-body {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-weight: var(--w-light);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .stances {
      margin: 1rem 0;
    }

    .stances div {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);
    }

    /* Care is the exception to the three neutralities, so it is set apart. */
    .stances .care {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--pink);
      background: #fff;
    }

    .stances .care dt {
      color: var(--ink-pink);
    }

    .stances dt {
      font-family: var(--heading);
      font-weight: var(--w-bold);
    }

    .stances dd {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-weight: var(--w-light);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .invite {
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: var(--fs-lead);
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .chain { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
      .chain li + li::before { content: '\2193'; left: 1rem; top: -1.35rem; }
      .stances div { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.2rem; }
      .anchors,
      .doors { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
      .lead-person { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('a.contact-button[data-u]').forEach((a) => {
      a.setAttribute('href', 'mailto:' + a.getAttribute('data-u') + '@' + a.getAttribute('data-d'));
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
